   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "CHEST PAIN",
   "bbox": [
    372.4,
    48.7,
    469.5,
    71.0
   ],
   "key": "p24-dffc02f6"
  },
  {
   "id": "p24-out-e02",
   "page": 24,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "1Chest pain caused by ischaemic heart disease. 2Dilute 10mg morphine with 9mL of sodium chloride 0.9%. Give diluted morphine 5mL IV over 5 minutes (1mL/minute). 3ST elevation > 1mm in two or more contiguous limb leads or ST elevation > 2mm in two or more contiguous chest leads. 4Discuss use of alteplase with a specialist/referral hospital. 5If SBP < 80, pulse ≥ 100, respiratory rate > 30, confusion/restlessness, weakness, shock likely. 6If severe penicillin allergy (previous angioedema, anaphylaxis or urticaria), discuss with doctor. Avoid giving Ringer's lactate together with IV ceftriaxone.",
